{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook","id":664730,"title":"What are the chances of a Black Spiral Dancer Tribebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-14T14:12:50-07:00","id":664730,"title":"What are the chances of a Black Spiral Dancer Tribebook?","content":"Sorry if this has been talked about before. Just wondering if there was any talk or chances regarding the matter.<br /> <br /> I know we have the Book of the Wyrm 20th Anniversary Edition, but I'm talking something more akin to your standard tribebook. I loved the White Howlers one we received through the Kickstarter and would love a BSD one in a similar manner.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 09-14-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T15:35:19-07:00","id":664908,"title":"","content":"There is one. It's called W20 Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T16:08:59-07:00","id":664990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=664908#post664908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one. It's called W20 Book of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Not what I was looking for.<br /> <br /> But thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T16:14:38-07:00","id":664997,"title":"","content":"You'd be off to a fantastic start just from using the splatbook for the most outright cruel and evil clan of vampires, whatever that one is. BSDs, for the most part, have the same tendency to wallow in self-indulgent cruelty and victimization or anyone within arm's reach. Then they add veneration of various evil totems on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T16:50:06-07:00","id":665053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=664997#post664997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd be off to a fantastic start just from using the splatbook for the most outright cruel and evil clan of vampires, whatever that one is. BSDs, for the most part, have the same tendency to wallow in self-indulgent cruelty and victimization or anyone within arm's reach. Then they add veneration of various evil totems on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that would be the Baali (They do the whole corrupting everyone and worshiping evil powers thing). Tzimisce are pretty nasty too but they don't really fit the bill quite as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7683-thesummerian","name":"TheSummerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T19:09:43-07:00","id":665209,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in such a book as well. The BSD's would combine certain elements of both Tzimisce and Baali vampires, maybe even the Sabbat in general. It's hard to say that the BSD's could be any worse than some of the vampires out there which are options to be played. Though W:tA has more of a good versus evil dynamic in the game, with the BSD's being more of the clear villains than are the Sabbat or Baali in V:tM. It seems like the ultra-evil vampires are portrayed in a more sympathetic light, at least in a way that one can understand where they are coming from, than the BSD's are. Though I think that is one reason why a BSD book interests me, because it could show things from a BSD perspective and make them more three dimensional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:55:45-07:00","id":665451,"title":"","content":"Ritualized rape, torture, and murder really needs expansion past what was in Book of the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> Now a Kinfolk book that revolves around 'fallen' shapechangers' kin might be a bit more useful.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T01:28:51-07:00","id":665463,"title":"","content":"Ethan Skemp used to say never. He's no longer the dev, and Onyx Path seems to be quite keen on giving the people what they want. On the other hand, one does have to wonder if in the current age with the sensibilities being as frail as they are, a book like that might not be very conductive to the image Onyx Path and CCP want to project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T06:36:18-07:00","id":665646,"title":"","content":"Do we need a tribe book beyond what has been printed in Book of the Wyrm 20? I'd rather that the limited space be used for other products, I'm quite capable of developing a hive of Spirals when I need one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:18:38-07:00","id":665670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook#post664730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been talked about before. Just wondering if there was any talk or chances regarding the matter.<br /> <br /> I know we have the Book of the Wyrm 20th Anniversary Edition, but I'm talking something more akin to your standard tribebook. I loved the White Howlers one we received through the Kickstarter and would love a BSD one in a similar manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the better question would be why Book of the wyrm 20th felt lacking to you as a BSD tribebook? What do you feel it wasnt touch upon/not expanded enough?<br /> <br /> Personally what i look in a tribebook is Gifts/merits/backgrounds/camps the rest is optional so to me Book of the wyrm is enough. What about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:27:02-07:00","id":665673,"title":"","content":"I want to know what does one get out of role-playing a bsd, or even running a bsd game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:34:47-07:00","id":665679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=665463#post665463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ethan Skemp used to say never. He's no longer the dev, and Onyx Path seems to be quite keen on giving the people what they want. On the other hand, one does have to wonder if in the current age with the sensibilities being as frail as they are, a book like that might not be very conductive to the image Onyx Path and CCP want to project.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't frail sensibilities. I'd say it's more acknowledging that there's no deep, hidden purpose to find in a sea of fecal matter. There's no shining treasure to be had, the giant mass of waste is pretty much as you see it all the way down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:51:06-07:00","id":665823,"title":"","content":"I think Book of the Wyrm did a pretty good job fleshing out whatever we need for BSD, even if you want to play one. Their mindet is described but their brutal and twisted activities are not, which is fine. A tribebook would provide more sordid and grisly details, and perhaps a smattering of more gifts? I don't really see the point- unless its sole purpose was to plumb the foetid depths of depravity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:58:04-07:00","id":665896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=665673#post665673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to know what does one get out of role-playing a bsd, or even running a bsd game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I merely would've liked to have seen a BSD Tribebook in the vein of the other tribebooks. No more, no less. Maybe I'd even play in a BSD-themed game.<br /> <br /> As for what I would get out of role-playing one? Probably the same amount of entertainment I get from playing other role-playing games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:32:39-07:00","id":666703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=665679#post665679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They aren't frail sensibilities. I'd say it's more acknowledging that there's no deep, hidden purpose to find in a sea of fecal matter. There's no shining treasure to be had, the giant mass of waste is pretty much as you see it all the way down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't like this enough. I tried to be civil as I know a statement like that would rile up a number of posters here, but that pretty much mirrors what I think about a potential BSD book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:32:23-07:00","id":667688,"title":"","content":"Not to play Devil(s advocate but what would be awesome would be an BSD chapter in an history supplement.<br /> <br /> I mean great defeats and victories of the Fallen Tribe., What were their goals and methods before Pentex entered the equation.<br /> <br /> A sort of Dark Revelations for the Wyrm (more like the Testament of Longinus than Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth) would be nice too.<br /> <br /> But a Tribebook that would make BSD playable? On one hand they did that with the Baali (and arguably with the Nefandi in Sorcerer's Crusade) so they could do that but I don't see the interest in playing a BSD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:03:27-07:00","id":668009,"title":"","content":"-sees a post on black spirals, checks the thread, sees a constant stream of &quot;they're bad people and nothing more.&quot;- so I see attitudes haven't changed much over 20 years.<br /> <br /> The spirals are garou too and deserve to have their stories told. I for one would like to see more rituals, examples of rites of the hunt twisted, or other such (interestingly the minds eye theater book of the wyrm has a massive section on it). <br /> <br /> Sure botw20th did great things for the spirals, but let's not pretend it's the same thing as a tribe book. Botw2nd had a comprehensive history of the tribe up until the 90's, including corruption of other tribes, and it didn't have to go into dodgy rape detail. <br /> <br /> Clearly by modern times the tribe evolved to be less like the wolf monsters we knew in earlier editions, into something more akin to fantasy vampires, living in lofts and taking the human herd for granted. I for one would love to see the transition, to see the tension between old hardliner bsds and the new blood that believes it's already won. <br /> <br /> The fact that the majority of you (story tellers and players alike) cannot fathom a bsd tribe book as anything other than... What was it... A fecal pit? Is a bit showing. Where's your imagination? What about the spiral strike team fighting against pentex' mockery breeds? What of the spirals corrupting churches to spread the wyrm? I thought there was a subtly to wyrm corruption? The way people treat spirals here, you'd think they were all mindless monsters without any brain power behind their actions.<br /> <br /> Botw20th was fantastic for gifts, as well as modernizing and improving the tribe expanetionally (as 20th has been for everything else), but it didn't touch on the customs near as much as Id like. I find it hard to believe the entirety of their existence is &quot;rape rape and more rape.&quot; You don't win wars like that. <br /> <br /> That's my 2 cents on the matter. I also may want really badass Ron spencer art of a spiral wearing a grizzly bear spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:43:51-07:00","id":668050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=668009#post668009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-sees a post on black spirals, checks the thread, sees a constant stream of &quot;they're bad people and nothing more.&quot;-<br /> <br /> The fact that the majority of you (story tellers and players alike) cannot fathom a bsd tribe book as anything other than... What was it... A fecal pit? Is a bit showing. Where's your imagination? What about the spiral strike team fighting against pentex' mockery breeds? What of the spirals corrupting churches to spread the wyrm? I thought there was a subtly to wyrm corruption? The way people treat spirals here, you'd think they were all mindless monsters without any brain power behind their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the most part I was content reading this post but I do have to comment on this. As a GM I don't need a tribe book to spark my imagination when it comes to these sorts of plots. I've already ran plots with Spiral priests leading human cults, and had an arch where my players were stuck in the middle of a Anurana/Spiral fued (the frogs were stealing spiral kin). None of this requires a tribe book past what BotW has provided (with W20 really doing a great job at it compared to earlier versions). For me its a matter of keeping the Spirals separate. Are they werewolves? Yes, but a stand alone tribe book I feel would grant an authenticity to them that makes players go &quot;See they are meant to be played&quot;, and from there I think would cause them to lose some of the evil. I don't need a tribe book to create 3D spirals for me, past source material and my own mind can do that without a problem (from the nihilist, to the Spiral who thinks she embodies the Garou's karma). I worry that a tribe book will try to humanize them too much and turn them in to &quot;I'm just misunderstood&quot; type concepts.<br /> <br /> For me the Spirals aren't &quot;misunderstood outsiders&quot; who need their tail told in anymore detail than the BotW, they're not Ronin, they are instead the monsters that go bump in the Garou's night. For that, along with the others stuff people mentioned (Just how evil the actions of Spirals can be) a tribe book isn't needed and probably shouldn't be. But that's my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:21:30-07:00","id":668223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=668009#post668009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-sees a post on black spirals, checks the thread, sees a constant stream of &quot;they're bad people and nothing more.&quot;- so I see attitudes haven't changed much over 20 years.<br /> <br /> The spirals are garou too and deserve to have their stories told. I for one would like to see more rituals, examples of rites of the hunt twisted, or other such (interestingly the minds eye theater book of the wyrm has a massive section on it).<br /> <br /> Sure botw20th did great things for the spirals, but let's not pretend it's the same thing as a tribe book. Botw2nd had a comprehensive history of the tribe up until the 90's, including corruption of other tribes, and it didn't have to go into dodgy rape detail.<br /> <br /> Clearly by modern times the tribe evolved to be less like the wolf monsters we knew in earlier editions, into something more akin to fantasy vampires, living in lofts and taking the human herd for granted. I for one would love to see the transition, to see the tension between old hardliner bsds and the new blood that believes it's already won.<br /> <br /> The fact that the majority of you (story tellers and players alike) cannot fathom a bsd tribe book as anything other than... What was it... A fecal pit? Is a bit showing. Where's your imagination? What about the spiral strike team fighting against pentex' mockery breeds? What of the spirals corrupting churches to spread the wyrm? I thought there was a subtly to wyrm corruption? The way people treat spirals here, you'd think they were all mindless monsters without any brain power behind their actions.<br /> <br /> Botw20th was fantastic for gifts, as well as modernizing and improving the tribe expanetionally (as 20th has been for everything else), but it didn't touch on the customs near as much as Id like. I find it hard to believe the entirety of their existence is &quot;rape rape and more rape.&quot; You don't win wars like that.<br /> <br /> That's my 2 cents on the matter. I also may want really badass Ron spencer art of a spiral wearing a grizzly bear spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You pretty much said my exact feelings on this; just far more intelligently than I ever could.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:18:01-07:00","id":668274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=668009#post668009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-sees a post on black spirals, checks the thread, sees a constant stream of &quot;they're bad people and nothing more.&quot;- so I see attitudes haven't changed much over 20 years.<br /> <br /> The spirals are garou too and deserve to have their stories told. I for one would like to see more rituals, examples of rites of the hunt twisted, or other such (interestingly the minds eye theater book of the wyrm has a massive section on it).<br /> <br /> Sure botw20th did great things for the spirals, but let's not pretend it's the same thing as a tribe book. Botw2nd had a comprehensive history of the tribe up until the 90's, including corruption of other tribes, and it didn't have to go into dodgy rape detail.<br /> <br /> Clearly by modern times the tribe evolved to be less like the wolf monsters we knew in earlier editions, into something more akin to fantasy vampires, living in lofts and taking the human herd for granted. I for one would love to see the transition, to see the tension between old hardliner bsds and the new blood that believes it's already won.<br /> <br /> The fact that the majority of you (story tellers and players alike) cannot fathom a bsd tribe book as anything other than... What was it... A fecal pit? Is a bit showing. Where's your imagination? What about the spiral strike team fighting against pentex' mockery breeds? What of the spirals corrupting churches to spread the wyrm? I thought there was a subtly to wyrm corruption? The way people treat spirals here, you'd think they were all mindless monsters without any brain power behind their actions.<br /> <br /> Botw20th was fantastic for gifts, as well as modernizing and improving the tribe expanetionally (as 20th has been for everything else), but it didn't touch on the customs near as much as Id like. I find it hard to believe the entirety of their existence is &quot;rape rape and more rape.&quot; You don't win wars like that.<br /> <br /> That's my 2 cents on the matter. I also may want really badass Ron spencer art of a spiral wearing a grizzly bear spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it has ever been a question whether or not they are intelligent. BOTW20 showed that well enough. These are smart creatures, no doubt about it.<br /> <br /> But why I think they should not be playable -especially- with the newest Wyrmbook, is where those smarts are used.<br /> <br /> All the tribes in the garou Nation, even the darker ones like Shadow Lords or Red Talons, still do have a goal to save the earth. Yes, they all have a different take on it, and it can be bad for humanity. But they still want to do good in their own way.<br /> <br /> BSDs, especially the botw20 ones, have the goal to worsen the world. No longer do they fight to redeem or rescue the wyrm. They do what they do to further the corruption of the world.<br /> <br /> And, at least for me as a player, there is no joy in taking those actions. I corrupted a church, and now the people worshipping there are worse off. Yay? With the Gaians, you at least can try to make the world a better place, even if its covered in blood and offal.<br /> <br /> Its the same reason why I don't really see the point of Sabbat games, I don't find joy out of makings things worse than they all ready are. And I think that's the reason why the WtA writers avoid making a BSD tb.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with them being rapey or mindless monsters, Its what they stand -for-.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:21:44-07:00","id":668281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=668009#post668009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-sees a post on black spirals, checks the thread, sees a constant stream of &quot;they're bad people and nothing more.&quot;- so I see attitudes haven't changed much over 20 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really need to. They're quite a great deal more extreme than the Sabbat, after all. Their end goal isn't to rule, but to break everything forever and revel in being destroyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spirals are garou too and deserve to have their stories told. I for one would like to see more rituals, examples of rites of the hunt twisted, or other such (interestingly the minds eye theater book of the wyrm has a massive section on it). </div> </div> </div>At that point it just becomes a catalog of opposite day rites, though. They make pits during the waning of the moon, they go out of their way to be horribly savage to prey during hunts and then insult it after killing it in horrid fashion, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure botw20th did great things for the spirals, but let's not pretend it's the same thing as a tribe book. Botw2nd had a comprehensive history of the tribe up until the 90's, including corruption of other tribes, and it didn't have to go into dodgy rape detail. </div> </div> </div>It did go into at least a little detail, though. Page 86 - 87 present a situation where BSDs are well known for kidnapping people to use as breeding stock and for institutionalized sexual abuse of lower-ranking BSDs. It's always present, hanging over everything, even if it doesn't get constantly re-emphasized (and didn't really need to be, honestly, because that would just waste word count when we already get the idea).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clearly by modern times the tribe evolved to be less like the wolf monsters we knew in earlier editions, into something more akin to fantasy vampires, living in lofts and taking the human herd for granted. I for one would love to see the transition, to see the tension between old hardliner bsds and the new blood that believes it's already won. </div> </div> </div>You can't be a vampire-like kind of person if you have Rage, though. It kind of puts a damper on the smooth operation of schemes when you're always orders of magnitude angrier than Henry Rollins. Always. In retrospect, this is actually a pretty deep flaw in W20 BotW. You don't want BSDs to be too smooth, or they stop looking like corrupt Garou and become like Vampwolves, or one of the other corrupted Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that the majority of you (story tellers and players alike) cannot fathom a bsd tribe book as anything other than... What was it... A fecal pit? Is a bit showing. Where's your imagination? What about the spiral strike team fighting against pentex' mockery breeds? What of the spirals corrupting churches to spread the wyrm? I thought there was a subtly to wyrm corruption? The way people treat spirals here, you'd think they were all mindless monsters without any brain power behind their actions. </div> </div> </div>The BSDs have a hard struggle to go through to try and be subtle influences of the Wyrm. They have all of the same failings and vulnerabilities of the Garou other than their code of ethics. That's a rather huge mountain of failings, and one that makes them far less adept at planning, strategy, and maneuvering than, say, Hatar, Kumo, and Bitter Grins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Botw20th was fantastic for gifts, as well as modernizing and improving the tribe expanetionally (as 20th has been for everything else), but it didn't touch on the customs near as much as Id like. I find it hard to believe the entirety of their existence is &quot;rape rape and more rape.&quot; You don't win wars like that.<br /> <br /> That's my 2 cents on the matter. I also may want really badass Ron spencer art of a spiral wearing a grizzly bear spirit. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need to be &quot;rape rape rape&quot; to not really be a burning necessity of word count to a lot of people. If it's just going to be nega-rites, that's something that can be handled with a paragraph, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:51:00-07:00","id":668675,"title":"","content":"Celt your wisdom is always good, but I don't necessarily want one for the playing purpose, more just to have a comprehensive lore of the tribe itself. <br /> <br /> Fact is there is a lot of lore on the spirals throughout 20 years of books, I would love it put in one place. Instead of &quot;howlers fell and now they're bastards,&quot; we could have something like a telling of just what the hell they were doing before the got to mexico, when they're power arguably began to sky rocket.<br /> <br /> As an aside saurops, LOVE the adapted vampishness of the new spirals. It showcases a change in mentality, and highlights one of the aspects that lets them beat the garou nation hand over foot. They change. They also happen to think there's no apocalypse either, which is its own mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T22:22:06-07:00","id":671675,"title":"","content":"Tribebook for BDS would be good, if a good job is done, that is, if it is well written. I agree in part with CeltSPZ, in:&quot; will try to humanize them too much and turn them in to &quot;I'm just misunderstood&quot; type concepts&quot;. for this i think this book It will not be written. I'd rather see the Wyrm as the dark side force, Werewolf is a starwars with Nihilism for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3958-silverb","name":"Silverb","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3958_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:29:54-07:00","id":673372,"title":"","content":"Tribebook: Black Spiral Dancer would be great as a way of celebrating Black Dog Games anniversary.<br /> <br /> Also I have played BSDs and have played in a BSD campaign. We did it with no rape fantasy or weird sexual fetishes. There's a whole lot more to the BSD than some raping McRaper BSD. In fact if that is what someone is presenting me I'd be more worried about them than any monstrous Garou. For now I'd say just stick with the various Book of the Wyrm supplements and the Chronicles of the Black Labrynthe chapbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:35:19-07:00","id":673480,"title":"","content":"Rape aside, how is a hundred pages of making people's lives horrible messes and enjoying when they finnally snap in any way mandatory reading material? We know what the Wyrm and the Spirals do We don't need to have a whole book about the nitty gritty first person view of their lifestyle and practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:41:16-07:00","id":673537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673372#post673372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribebook: Black Spiral Dancer would be great as a way of celebrating Black Dog Games anniversary.<br /> <br /> Also I have played BSDs and have played in a BSD campaign. We did it with no rape fantasy or weird sexual fetishes. There's a whole lot more to the BSD than some raping McRaper BSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, with all due respect, you weren't doing the Wyrm's children justice. Pretty much all Black Spiral Dancers are rape-ier than a pent-up 17th century buccaneer, and that is saying a lot. Sanitizing the fallen Garou is pretty much necessary to make them even approach playability. The dark hints at the worst excesses of the Black Spiral Dancers (as Saur Ops mentioned on pg 87) are not meant to make you want to play the fucked up things- you are meant to want to KILL THEM.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rape is horrible, but throughout history it has also been shockingly, monstrously common. Recently (last few decades or so) we have collectively and rightly decided that it is a horrible moral crime and should be stopped and prevented. However, rape isn't some special crime or sin to Whipporwhill's kids- but it doesn't have to be a glorious act of service to the Wyrm either. Rape is not something the Spirals see as a critical part of what they are- they just take what they want, nothing more, and certainly nothing less. Whether that is territory or a new shotgun or a pretty human... it doesn't matter to them; they are strong, so they do what they will to the weak. And, in my opinion, that callousness just makes it <i>worse</i><i>!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-21-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T20:06:11-07:00","id":673814,"title":"","content":"And yet there's an entire book about playing fomori...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T21:00:27-07:00","id":673835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673480#post673480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rape aside, how is a hundred pages of making people's lives horrible messes and enjoying when they finnally snap in any way mandatory reading material? We know what the Wyrm and the Spirals do We don't need to have a whole book about the nitty gritty first person view of their lifestyle and practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying it's mandatory reading material. A lot of the books that OP produces across its various lines are not mandatory. If you don't want it, don't buy it. Don't read it. But please, stop speaking for me. You don't want a BSD book. I think everyone gets that.<br /> <br /> But some would like it. This thread makes that pretty clear, I'd say. The Baali have a clanbook. The Fomori have an entire book dedicated to them. As does Pentex.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the harm in making a BSD clanbook for use in Werewolf games. Hopefully one of the developers feels the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T21:11:44-07:00","id":673842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673814#post673814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet there's an entire book about playing fomori...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fomori 1) used to be something else, as long as they aren't ferectoi, and 2) are acknowledge to not be long-lasting characters in typical games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T21:32:22-07:00","id":673849,"title":"","content":"Oh oh oh can I get my players guide to nephandi after that?...../sarcasm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T22:10:27-07:00","id":673861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673849#post673849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh oh oh can I get my players guide to nephandi after that?...../sarcasm</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think that be a great option to have! After all, this is the World of Darkness. I don't see anything wrong will role-playing an evil character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T01:06:25-07:00","id":673930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673814#post673814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet there's an entire book about playing fomori...</div> </div> </div> </div>That book is pretty much the summation why we don't need a BSD book. It's a one off joke book that's mostly used for cheap shock value. The whole book even says that it's not meant to be taken seriously as it's an exercise in disposable splatterpunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T02:20:29-07:00","id":673976,"title":"","content":"Actually a player guide to Nephandi has been published it's called Infernalism the Path of Screams and it's better than it sounds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T02:52:02-07:00","id":673996,"title":"","content":"Infernalists can be Nephandi, but most of them are not. Also, do note that that book is an analytical third person look at what people percieve to be infernalism and on its effect on society. In no way does it support or condone the acts of infernalists and it takes great pains to show them as deluded fools without ever stopping to explain how you should play one (as a player) and what they actually have to say on the matter.<br /> <br /> That's quite different from a tribebook, which is always a in character account of a group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 09-22-2015, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T03:33:18-07:00","id":674018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=673814#post673814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet there's an entire book about playing fomori...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was pretty much considered a bad idea after the fact, and so when 'Revised' came around, we got 'Possessed' as a whole, including all three of the Triat's servants + Gaia's own and cutting a few sleazier edges off.\u200b<br /> <br /> In fact, that was the \u200brequest from the fans on the official mailing list.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:19:00-07:00","id":674087,"title":"","content":"To take this to another direction, what -would- a BSD tribebook offer that we don't all ready have in BOTW's editions?<br /> <br /> We have history, we have in-character accounts on tribes from both a born bsd and a converted one that paint both as intelligent people, we have rites and gifts, we have sample NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T06:22:37-07:00","id":674115,"title":"","content":"Yes we do, but the problem is its spread across several books. Let's not forget table top isn't exactly a cheap hobby, and some people don't have a spare 120+$ laying around to purchase up all the necessary material to get the equivalent.<br /> <br /> As for new content? The missing 1500+ years of the spiral existence where they lived underground and did... Well no one knows. They were just some dark evil joke up until they hit mexico, and as a fan of lore in general I would like to know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T07:41:49-07:00","id":674191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=674115#post674115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes we do, but the problem is its spread across several books. Let's not forget table top isn't exactly a cheap hobby, and some people don't have a spare 120+$ laying around to purchase up all the necessary material to get the equivalent.<br /> <br /> As for new content? The missing 1500+ years of the spiral existence where they lived underground and did... Well no one knows. They were just some dark evil joke up until they hit mexico, and as a fan of lore in general I would like to know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the 2nd edition BotW, they were tunneling around and attempting to get out of Europe, because in those days, their enemies, the default and technically optional PC types, were not so heinously disadvantaged and would probably have been able to crush them, since they were the remnants of a small, isolationist tribe that had just mauled itself, killing all of those who did not convert. Being so hemmed in, it took a while to break out and not become like BattleTech's Clan Blood Spirit (RIP 3085).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:02:00-07:00","id":679490,"title":"","content":"I remeber this coming up long before we even got W20 as an idea. We were told back in the day we'd never get a BSD tribe book beyond the Book of the Wyrm. Even with the Black Dog label I got the impression that an indepth exploration would beyond the pale in terms depraved mortality (or lack there of).<br /> <br /> However i do remeber asking for one at the tail end of the revised WtA line as a BSD novel in my mind opened up the chance for a tribe book. In retrospect it wouldn't be needed and while I am blown away that we now have a White Howler book I still don't expect a BSD tribe book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T19:06:43-07:00","id":680589,"title":"","content":"I Think Book of the Wyrms ALL we need For a tribe book...<br /> <br /> And I know its bad form, but time or two years ago met some people on chats who play BSD's And I couldnt help lecturing them.<br /> <br /> As the BSD's are simply and purely EVIL<br /> <br /> their not really fighting to save the world, their not using methods they dont like their monsters pure and simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:52:04-07:00","id":681419,"title":"","content":"And yet people play games like manhunt and grand theft auto. <br /> <br /> A touch on the comment that this has come up before, if such is the case why do we assume there isn't a demand for it? It's not a question of need but a want. If you don't want it that's fine, but I'd rather have the option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:20:38-07:00","id":681510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=680589#post680589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Think Book of the Wyrms ALL we need For a tribe book...<br /> <br /> And I know its bad form, but time or two years ago met some people on chats who play BSD's And I couldnt help lecturing them.<br /> <br /> As the BSD's are simply and purely EVIL<br /> <br /> their not really fighting to save the world, their not using methods they dont like <b>their monsters pure and simple</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the <b>World of Darkness</b>. 95% of everything you play as or against is a monster. There are plenty of light-hearted role-playing games out there. I've seen a few posts like yours recently, that makes me wonder if the fans that are saying this are the same ones that grew up with White Wolf's World of Darkness in the 90's, or are they newer fans?<br /> <br /> Regardless, as LoW stated, this may not be something for everyone. But it's pretty clear from here and on other forums and various social media sites, that there IS a want for this that I didn't know existed much before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:50:17-07:00","id":681632,"title":"","content":"What I find more amusing, is there seems to be a love of playable bale hounds in forsaken, which are arguably the same thing, and yet here, apocalypse people abhor the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 09-29-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T21:12:49-07:00","id":681735,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds pass with less notice in the nWoD because they dialed up the personal scale crapness in the world and played down wider-ranging impacts of a lot of actions. These are not things that W:tA does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=681510#post681510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the <b>World of Darkness</b>. 95% of everything you play as or against is a monster. There are plenty of light-hearted role-playing games out there. I've seen a few posts like yours recently, that makes me wonder if the fans that are saying this are the same ones that grew up with White Wolf's World of Darkness in the 90's, or are they newer fans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Monster might have been used clumsily in this case, but even back in the good old bad old days of the 90s, there was recognition of a line between &quot;monsters to humans&quot; and &quot;monsters to the core thesis of the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless, as LoW stated, this may not be something for everyone. But it's pretty clear from here and on other forums and various social media sites, that there IS a want for this that I didn't know existed much before. </div> </div> </div>A lot of people seem to want it because they see the BSDs as Sabbat equivalent instead of what they are actually equivalent to in V:tM, Ultra-Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T07:03:20-07:00","id":682006,"title":"","content":"I own the Baali clanbook. I have a background in History and Anthropology. I have studied the Holocaust, South Africa, the Armenian genocide, and quite a bit of real world nastiness. The Baali clanbook gave me nightmares. The BSD book would be just as bad if not worse. I could easily run a BSD chronicle with the information in the Book of the Wyrm 20. I have no desire to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T08:00:43-07:00","id":682068,"title":"","content":"Wider ranging consequences of actions have a bigger impact in nwod. True it doesn't have an over arching evil, but If someone causes death that will taint the shadow. That action leads to an increase in similar as the spirits hunger for that essence and the spirit scape radically shifts. <br /> <br /> A better argument for it might be the moral objectivity of forsaken vs apocalypse' clear right and wrong stance (though in all honesty bale hounds are just strait bad).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T08:44:50-07:00","id":682114,"title":"","content":"I'ts funny the &quot;why BaleHound yes and Dancers not&quot; when they're the one and the same, the only difference is Dancers are an entire culture based around depravity and BaleHounds are individuals who are depraved.<br /> Playing a baby eater is the same if it come for a culture that revel in it or if is a mad man who pray to a mad god for power. <br /> <br /> The Dancers deserves it's own book, The baali and the Nephandi have it, Why the Dancers not?<br /> Book of the Wyrm20 is a cool resource book, but is too much Pentenx and no bite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:45:06-07:00","id":682217,"title":"","content":"Exactly this. Besides that, we could get into tandem operations with first teams and other fallen shifters. <br /> <br /> And let's not forget the first ronin, who at the least could use some coverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:44:30-07:00","id":682438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/664730-what-are-the-chances-of-a-black-spiral-dancer-tribebook?p=681735#post681735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to want it because they see the BSDs as Sabbat equivalent instead of what they are 